+/* Priority hand-off at thread creation (opt-in: ppu_thread_set_prio_handoff).
+ *
+ * lv2 schedules PPU threads by strict priority, lower number first. Creating a
+ * thread of HIGHER priority than the creator therefore preempts the creator on
+ * the spot: the new thread runs until it first blocks, and only then does
+ * sys_ppu_thread_create return. Titles lean on that. One that starts a
+ * high-priority service thread and then immediately uses what the thread sets
+ * up has no lock around it and needs none on a PS3.
+ *
