+/* PS3_PPU_PRIO_SCHED=<cores>: let the HOST scheduler stand in for lv2's.
+ *
+ * Confine every guest PPU thread to <cores> host cores (the PPU has two
+ * hardware threads, so 2 is the faithful value and 1 the strict one) and map
+ * guest priority onto host thread priority with dynamic boosting off. Among
+ * threads sharing a core Windows then runs the highest-priority ready one and
+ * preempts for it at once, which is the property titles rely on: a thread
+ * never observes a higher-priority one half-way through its work.
+ *
+ * The mapping is lossy -- seven host levels for 3072 guest ones -- so threads
+ * whose priorities fall in one band still interleave. Off by default. */
